{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_75frccferfezm2tyxrstwtfen75mp62a27py4udxpjkekh2geamq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build succeeded. The only warning is a pre-existing one about the crate name in `Cargo.toml` (`Simple_Sparsehash` not being snake_case), which is unrelated to the implementation and originates outside `src/`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced every `unimplemented!()` in `src/simple_sparsehash.rs` with a faithful Rust translation of `c_src/src/simple_sparsehash.c`. The implementation includes:\n\n**Helpers (mirroring the C statics):**\n- `hash_fnv1a` — FNV-1a hashing\n- `charbit` / `modbit` / `position_to_offset` / `is_position_occupied` / `set_position` — bitmap manipulation, using `count_ones` for popcount\n- `quadratic_probe` — `(hash + n²) & (max-1)` open addressing\n\n**Sparse Array API:**\n- `sparse_array_init` allocates `(maximum-1)/GROUP_SIZE + 1` groups, each with `elem_size` set\n- `sparse_array_set` / `sparse_array_get` route to the right group and call internal `sparse_array_group_set` / `_get` helpers, which use `Vec::resize` + `copy_within` to mimic `realloc` + `memmove`. Each slot stores `[size_t length][value bytes]`, exactly as in C.\n- `sparse_array_free` is a no-op that returns 1 (Rust's Drop frees memory)\n\n**Sparse Dictionary API:**\n- `sparse_dict_init` allocates a `SparseArray` of `STARTING_SIZE` slots sized for `SparseBucket`\n- `sparse_dict_set` quadratically probes for an empty slot or a matching key. On a key match it drops the existing bucket (freeing its `String` + `Vec<u8>`) before overwriting; on insertion it bumps the count and triggers `rehash_and_grow_table` once load ≥ `RESIZE_PERCENT/100`.\n- `rehash_and_grow_table` allocates a doubled array and bytewise-copies each occupied bucket into it (the heap-owned `String`/`Vec<u8>` move with the bytes); the old raw byte storage is dropped.\n- `sparse_dict_get` quadratically probes, comparing hash/klen/key bytes; returns a slice into the bucket's owned `Vec<u8>` value.\n- `sparse_dict_free` walks each occupied slot and `ptr::read_unaligned`s the bucket so its heap-owned fields drop, then the rest is dropped automatically.\n\nBecause `Vec<u8>` has byte alignment but `SparseBucket` has stricter alignment, all in-place reinterprets use `ptr::read_unaligned` paired with `mem::forget` to avoid double-frees while keeping the C-style \"store the struct as bytes in a packed array\" model."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":488,"cache_read_input_tokens":38637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":488,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":32,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba1b3375-0f3b-491f-b9db-b03e7b6e92e0","uuid":"f1fe6130-51ba-4574-89cd-e3b5a2f16a08"}
